# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
#
# EDB_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKEN is the credential for your EDB repositories. It is
# read from the environment at build time and passed to the build as a
# BuildKit secret, so it should never need to exist in a file here at all —
# but if you do keep it in .env, this is what stops it being committed.
#
# .env.example is the template and carries no values, so it is force-included.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.token
secrets.*

# Anything key-shaped, in case a certificate experiment ends up in the tree.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
credentials
credentials.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by cider itself
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `cider bootstrap` backs up your container config before editing it.
*.cider-press.*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
